{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456678-who-gets-the-paradox","id":1456678,"title":"Who gets the Paradox?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-12T09:30:02-07:00","id":1456678,"title":"Who gets the Paradox?","content":"Hi there<br /> <br /> Do non-awakened creatures get Paradox/Permadox for vulgar modifications made on their patterns? Or are the mages doing those modifications the one getting the Paradox/Permadox?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T09:42:40-07:00","id":1456679,"title":"","content":"None awakened creatures suffer from unbelief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T10:44:58-07:00","id":1456683,"title":"","content":"The non-Awakened can also suffer Pattern Bleed (and are very ill-equipped to do anything about it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T16:14:23-07:00","id":1456712,"title":"","content":"So, non-awakened cyborgs can go around with implants/improvements/robotic parts similar to the ones their awakened counterparts have, but without the permanent Paradox their awakened counterparts pay for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T16:27:47-07:00","id":1456715,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. However, that's not an advantage. As mentioned, they have to deal with unbelief and pattern bleed. In short, they have a distressing tendency to break down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T18:12:33-07:00","id":1456723,"title":"","content":"Where can I find the rules for Pattern Bleeding? In M20 it is mentioned once in the whole book and the explanation is not really that clear. <br /> <br /> As a result, an organism that has been radically<br /> altered by Life magick (given new limbs or other characteristics<br /> that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern) suffers Pattern<br /> bleeding: an inexorable Quintessence leak that inflicts one level<br /> of lethal damage per day. Unless the caster uses Prime magick<br /> to refill that Pattern with fresh energy, or alters that Pattern<br /> permanently, the damage continues until the subject dies.<br /> <br /> So, if I get 10 successes to make the alteration permanent, PB doesnt happen anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T01:41:22-07:00","id":1456740,"title":"","content":"I also remember something about cyborgs and similar applying their permanent paradox to nearby Mages or similar, but I can't remember the page reference. I think there's an idea in M20 along those lines but no idea where I'd find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T01:48:24-07:00","id":1456741,"title":"","content":"Here's what I want to know - would a Marauder cancel out Unbelief and Pattern Bleed with their &quot;Reality Sink&quot;. For instance a Marauder cyberneticist who was born out of a Denial quiet, would they be bending reality in such a way around them that their uncanny cyborgs were immune to the unbelief factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T04:35:06-07:00","id":1456747,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's come up before, but I would presume so. That is, if someone's otherwise paradoxical augmentation would fit well in a Marauder's altered reality they just get wrapped into it. The unbelief wouldn't disappear so much as it would be wrapped into the paradox the Marauder was generating and would release in the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T06:10:17-07:00","id":1456753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456678-who-gets-the-paradox?p=1456723#post1456723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I get 10 successes to make the alteration permanent, PB doesnt happen anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my understanding. That way you don't suffer Pattern Bleed anymore, but have Permanent Paradox instead<br /> <br /> However, Unbelief can cause a creature to become <i>Thaumnivore</i>. I think there's rules, or something close, for Thaumnivore in Gods &amp; Monsters - but it's basically &quot;pattern bleed&quot; (you eat Tass/Quintessence, or you start to die). And that has nothing to do with permanence<br /> <br /> You could also see the Genetic Flaws for biomods in M20. I think that those rules could be a neat way to houserule &quot;Permanent Paradox&quot; for those that don't cast spells, since it was built as an alternative of the permadox that cybernetics cause<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T06:50:36-07:00","id":1456756,"title":"","content":"That said: if a device generates paradox, then the device suffers the backlash. This can be generalized to enhance being suffering the backlash from whatever effects are built into them. Giving them Permadox is consistent with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-17T02:33:13-07:00","id":1457011,"title":"","content":"Pattern Bleed is mainly a problem if it's not a &quot;natural&quot; part of the person's pattern. If the pattern is twisted into a different shape in a significant (read: mechanically significant) way, that change needs to be sustained by Quintessence on a daily basis or suffer damage.<br /> <br /> However, if the alteration becomes a regular part of the person's pattern, it ceases to be something that causes Pattern Bleeding. Because it's not twisting the pattern, that's just how they are. (Granted, alterations of a clearly supernatural nature still cause Unbelief, but at least you aren't hemorrhaging Quint just to stay alive.)<br /> <br /> In game mechanics terms, this usually means buying these changes off with XP. What form that takes depend on the permanent Effect. It might be an integral Wonder/Enhancement, a Merit (and/or Flaw), an Advantage, or even just an Attribute score increase. Some characters increase their Strength by going to the gym and eating lots of protein. Mages can do it by brewing a potion of ox blood and rare herbs, to magically grow their muscles. If they spend the XP to get another dot, it's the same either way.<br /> <br /> Presumably, a cyborg working for the Technocracy has already spent all the XP (starting or otherwise) &quot;offscreen&quot; to justify having dots in the Enhancement background, or whatever. So at least in respect to Pattern Bleeding, they're good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T18:17:13-07:00","id":1457932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456678-who-gets-the-paradox#post1456678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there<br /> <br /> Do non-awakened creatures get Paradox/Permadox for vulgar modifications made on their patterns? Or are the mages doing those modifications the one getting the Paradox/Permadox?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC:<br /> <br /> Paradox goes to the caster, Permadox goes to the effect. Keep in mind they follow complementary, but distinct <u>rules</u>.<br /> <br /> A non-Mage won't get Paradox unless they somehow counts as caster for a spell. Theoretically an Adept of Prime can do this kind of shit.<br /> <br /> But if the non-mage is modified, then you must decide if it is a common Pattern Alteration, a permanent Pattern Alteration, or an implanted Wonder.<br /> <br /> Wonders can get Paradox for their effects normally, but their presence don't have to be a problem by itself. If the non-mage get an implanted flamethrower in the arm, then it is a Wonder and any Permadox is optional, but using the flamethrower causes Paradox normally. Pattern alteration may cause Pattern Bleeding if common or Permadox if permanent. Permadox won't do much to the non-mage most of the time, but still works in Mages around them. What is more, it can make the non-mage a valid target for Paradox Effects they wouldn't normally suffer from, at the ST discretion. Becoming a Thaumivore is also possible.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the other check on the alteration is the Paradox of the original casting. The non-mage don't get Paradox, but the mage doing the alteration does. It isn't common among the Traditions, but sometimes a Paradox Effect manifests as a &quot;glitch&quot; in the effect, and this glitch is as permanent as the effect itself, so even if those alterations don't attract Paradox directly, it doesn't mean they can't have attached disadvantages due to Paradox in their creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}